## Conversation
Part of a repo improvement sweep the user requested. Claude found that bashrc carried inline copies of the git aliases that configs/aliases/git had since hardened, and the user asked for the fix.

## Actions
Replaced the inline git alias block in configs/bashrc with sourcing of configs/aliases/git, resolving the repo dir via readlink -f on BASH_SOURCE. Verified with bash -n and by sourcing aliases/git in a bash subshell (gcm/gpum/gpom/wt all defined).

