None

## Dead Ends
The obvious fix (loop over the whole aliases/ dir like zshrc does) was rejected: aliases/k8s uses compdef and oh-my-zsh's $ZSH completions dir, which fail under bash.

## Hints for Future Agents
bashrc is Linux/WSL/container-only (macOS installs zshrc), so GNU readlink -f is safe. bashrc still has its own inline k8s aliases; deduplicating them means splitting aliases/k8s into portable and zsh-only parts. bash gains the wt worktree function from the shared file.

## Codebase Discoveries
configs/aliases/git claims it is "sourced by both bash and zsh" but bashrc did not source it until this commit.

